From 415a408af1ec6b8a02127af9cfabfcbf4a830896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:35:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 57/97] kernel: W5 stub audit - device info reports
 FILE_DEVICE_DISK; XCTD keeps INVALID_PARAMETER with caller diagnostics;
 XNetLogonGetTitleID and XAM message dispatch log caller once

- NtQueryVolumeInformationFile(XFileFsDeviceInformation): FILE_DEVICE_DISK (only caller, the title's utility-drive
  mount, tests == 0x46 EHSTOR: same branch as before); unit test pins 0x7.
- NtQueryInformationFile(XFileXctdCompressionInformation): stays X_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER (= Xenia Canary); the
  caller (sub_82B8AB00 via sub_82B8AA98) then checks the file's own XCTD magic 0x0FF512ED. Once-per-session WARN with
  guest LR and path (path built inside call_once).
- IoDismountVolumeByFileHandle: documented intentional no-op (return ignored by the caller).
- XNetLogonGetTitleID: behaves exactly like the stub (r3 preserved) but logs each (caller LR, selector) once; XAM
  message dispatch logs each (app, message, result, LR) once. Runtime (build 3ce91bfa): only caller is the Live
  sign-in-gated sub_82CB78F0; no app 0xFC message offline.
Evidence: docs/KERNEL-STUBS-W5.md (game repo). Reviewer: XCTD/device/dismount accepted; final round found no defect
(procedural INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE: its gate ran on ace1524b, which contains this code - PASS); unit tests [kernel]
74/74 assertions, [system] 28/28 run by the coordinator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
